# CI/CD & Release Readiness

## Quality gates

New or modified code must pass without errors or warnings:

- Typecheck: `npx tsc --noEmit`
- Lint: `npm run lint` (`expo lint`)

No unused imports, unexplained `eslint-disable`, or `@ts-expect-error` without a comment.

## Cross-platform

- Behavior must work on iOS and Android. Use `Platform.select` or `.ios.ts` / `.android.ts` when native APIs differ.
- Touch targets ≥ 44pt. Set `accessibilityRole` / `accessibilityLabel` on icon-only and primary CTAs.
- Keyboard: `keyboardShouldPersistTaps="handled"`; do not cover inputs with the tab bar / FAB.
- RevenueCat native SDK is not available in Expo Go — keep DEV override paths; do not assume IAP works in Go.

## Testable structure

- Keep domain logic in `lib/` (stores, `api`, validators) so Jest can cover it without rendering screens.
- Hooks (`usePolling`, `useMounted`) must clean up intervals/subscriptions.
- Loading / empty / error states on every network-facing screen.

Do not add dependencies unless necessary and Expo SDK 54 compatible. API JSON contracts are shared with `flipon` — breaking shapes requires updating both apps.
